<workflow>
  <name>main-0059-synchronize-after-merge-batch-error-accounting</name>
  <name_sync_with_filename>Y</name_sync_with_filename>
  <description>Synchronize after merge with an error hop on PostgreSQL, twelve rows at commit size 5: updates, inserts and deletes, a row to skip, and three rows the database refuses: the update of 2 (check constraint, in the middle of the first commit window), the insert of 5 (duplicate key, first row of the second window) and the delete of 6 (a child row refers to it). Once with batch updates on: PostgreSQL's validated batch failure contract (the whole batch is lost) keeps batching on with the error hop, without a savepoint per row, and the good rows of a failed batch are run again. Once with batch updates off: every row runs behind a savepoint and is passed on right after it, as before. Asserts for both that exactly the three bad rows reach the error stream, with the error code of their path, that the other rows are written and reported once, and that no row is reported on the main output unless what it did is in the table.</description>
  <extended_description/>
  <workflow_version/>
  <created_user>-</created_user>
  <created_date>2026/11/27 12:00:00.000</created_date>
  <modified_user>-</modified_user>
  <modified_date>2026/11/27 12:00:00.000</modified_date>
  <parameters>
    </parameters>
  <actions>
    <action>
      <name>Start</name>
      <description/>
      <type>SPECIAL</type>
      <attributes/>
